 that you have free food and accommodation on board, you have the possibility to earn and most important to save a lot of money during a contract. The contracts vary from seven to ten months, depending on ship schedule you are assigned to. In some cases, the travel to join the vessel, has to be paid out of your own pocket (train or taxi), but you will be reimbursed for any travel expenses once you are onboard.\nCompany’s will pay for your return trip, at the completion of the contract.\nOn a personal level, you should be very flexible, fully motivated, team orientated and open for new challenges and experiences. You should be able to use the new experiences combined with your professional background and knowledge, in the daily operation on board. An education in the Hotel business and some years of experience, is also one of the conditions to be a candidate for an onboard position. Good to excellent knowledge of the English or German language is a must, any additional language would be considered a plus.\nWhat Documents Do I Need To Join The Ship?\nBefore joining a Cruise ship, there are several preparations to take care of, from eventually needed visas and medical examinations by your local doctor. You will also need a passport valid for min. 12 more months.\nWe will provide you with detailed information, what you need, where and how to get it and what in particular to look out for. River Crew Agency will assist you to with all preparations and will be available for you at any time.\nDue to our own experience of working on board ocean and river ships, and being in the recruiting business for some time now, we at Agency will give you all our experience and knowledge to help you and assist you to prepare all your documents and will be always available for any questions you have.","tokens":["A"," passenger"," on"," a"," Cruise"," Ship"," expects"," excellent"," Food",","," Dr","inks"," and"," Service",","," at"," any"," area"," and"," at"," any"," time",","," day"," o