to":[],"attention_weights":[],"max_activation":1.1782557964324951,"max_token_index":286,"peak_labels":{"hate speech":"none","language":"en","names":"none","part of speech":"PROPN","personal data":"none","postal addresses":"none","source":"c4","toxicity":"none"},"text":"Director of Development and Business Affairs Manager at Sarrazin Couture Entertainment, Vivian Lin is an alumna of the CMPA National Mentorship program and Sheridan College’s Advanced Film and Television, and has obtained her Certificate of Entertainment Law from Osgoode Hall Law School.\nShe recently associate produced the pilot Stay with Me for CTV, a $2.8 million legal drama starring Andrea Roth (Rescue Me) and is currently co-producing Sarrazin Couture’s feature film Four One Nine.\nLin’s production credits include production managing the feature film promo American Royalty, and production coordinating and script coordinating the 8 x 30min CityTV series Meet the Family. Directing credits include the short film And They Watched, a horror morality tale, the eight-episode webseries Pretty in Geek, the short film Four Walls starring Nina Dobrev (Vampire Diaries) and Brendan Jeffers (Degrassi: TNG), and the play The Mirror, which premiered at the Montreal Fringe Festival.\nShe has completed the University of Toronto’s Writing Episodic Television II, Comedy Bar’s Episodic Comedy Writing Room course, Second City’s Comedy Writing and Improvisation courses. Lin has a background in both production and broadcasting.\nLin is also the Vice-Hub of the Producers Roundtable of Ontario (PRO).","tokens":["Director"," of"," Development"," and"," Business"," Affairs"," Manager"," at"," Sar","raz","in"," C","out","ure"," Entertainment",","," Viv","ian"," Lin"," is"," an"," al","um","na"," of"," the"," C","MP","A"," National"," Ment","orship"," program"," and"," Sher","idan"," College","’","s"," Advanced"," Film"," and"," Television",","," and"," has"," obtained"," her"," Certificate"," of"," Entertainment"," Law"," fr